{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed168776016/4/codegen_prompts/6.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/4`\n- 题号：`6`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed168776016/4/6.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"6\">\n- `description`：根据每个彩色对象内部孔洞的形状，在网格边缘的图例区中找到匹配的模板，然后用图例指定的颜色重绘该对象的外轮廓。\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（如 black）。\n  - 网格顶部有一行\"图例区\"：由若干个小方块组成，每个小方块内部有一个独特的小型镂空图案（孔洞形状），小方块的边框颜色各不相同（如 red、blue、green 等）。图例小方块之间用背景色间隔。\n  - 网格下方主区域中散布着若干个较大的单色前景对象（颜色为 grey），每个对象是一个实心的不规则形状，但内部恰好有一个由背景色构成的孔洞。\n  - 每个对象内部孔洞的形状与图例区中某个小方块内的镂空图案形状完全一致（可能经过平移但不旋转不翻转）。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对主区域中的每个 grey 对象，提取其内部孔洞的形状。\n  - 在图例区中找到孔洞形状与之匹配的小方块。\n  - 将该 grey 对象的所有像素重新染成匹配小方块的边框颜色。\n  - 图例区保持不变，孔洞保持为背景色。\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要首先注意到对象内部的孔洞并非随意形状，而是与图例中的模板存在精确对应；然后需要通过形状匹配（而非位置、大小或数量）建立对象与图例之间的映射关系——孔洞作为\"隐藏签名\"的角色是核心洞见。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：eval/a25697e4, train/99caaf76, train/8a6d367c, eval/62593bfd, train/df9fd884, eval/e3721c99, eval/898e7135, eval/a32d8b75\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"a25697e4\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3759\nmechanism=0.4604\nlexical=0.0140\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:counter, code:rotation, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:hole, object:sprite, operation:count, operation:rotate, operation:shape_match, operation:translate, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/a25697e4.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/a25697e4.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nDock movable tools into border-anchored frames by filling cavities.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Border-touching components cluster into anchor frames with interior bg cavities.\n- Non-border 2-color components are movable tools.\n\nRule:\n- Match each tool to a frame whose cavity size equals one of its color-region counts.\n- Rotate/flip the tool so one color fills the cavity exactly; the other stays outside.\n- If the docking orientation uses a reflection, swap the tool's two colors.\n\nKey insight: Cavity size determines tool–frame pairing; reflection triggers color swap.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"sprite s not touching the edges\",\n  \"dst\": \"dock into frames d on edge\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.component.shape == d.notch.shape with rotation/flip\",\n  \"transform\": \"swap colors of the two components of s if flip is used\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"99caaf76\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3398\nmechanism=0.3940\nlexical=0.0166\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:counter, code:rotation, object:grid_edge, object:hole, object:sprite, operation:rotate, operation:translate, output:same_size, relation:direction, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/99caaf76.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/99caaf76.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nMove each marked cross object away from its marker to the grid edge while rotating the colored cross 180 degrees.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Each 8-connected foreground object has nine pixels: a 4-pixel marker-color\n  sprite attached to a 5-pixel non-marker colored cross.\n- Each object bbox is either 3x6 or 6x3, so the marker sprite is on exactly\n  one side of the cross.\n\nRule:\n- Move the whole object straight away from its marker side until the object\n  bbox touches the corresponding grid edge.\n- Keep the marker sprite unchanged within the object.\n- Rotate the 3x3 colored cross block by 180 degrees before placing it.\n\nKey insight:\nThe marker sprite is a directional tail; the cross is the leading payload,\nand only that payload turns around during the slide to the edge.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"each 8-connected composite object made of a 4-pixel blue marker sprite attached to a 5-pixel colored cross\",\n  \"path\": \"straight away from the marker sprite until the composite bbox reaches the grid edge\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"move the whole composite rigidly along that path\",\n  \"transform\": \"rotate the 3x3 colored cross 180 degrees within the composite; keep the marker sprite unchanged\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"8a6d367c\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3192\nmechanism=0.4149\nlexical=0.0139\ncode_feature=0.2857\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:hole, object:sprite, object:square, object:template, operation:count, operation:translate, relation:direction, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/8a6d367c.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/8a6d367c.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nComplete the framed area by expanding the unique upper template that contains the existing seed pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- A teal background contains small colored template masks above a larger rectangular frame.\n- The frame encloses one fill color arranged as a partial block-scaled copy of one template.\n- The frame interior dimensions are an integer square scale of the matching template bbox.\n\nRule:\n- Crop to the rectangular frame.\n- Identify the unique upper template whose block-scaled mask covers every existing fill pixel inside the frame.\n- Reset the frame interior to background and paint the whole scaled mask with the fill color.\n\nKey insight:\nThe lower colored pixels are seed cells that reveal which upper template should be completed inside the frame.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"upper colored template mask s\",\n  \"dst\": \"rectangular frame interior d containing partial fill-color seed pixels\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"block-scaled s contains all seed pixels in d\",\n  \"transform\": \"clear dst to bg and paint the full matched scaled mask with the seed color\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"crop to the rectangular frame\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"62593bfd\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3579\nmechanism=0.4215\nlexical=0.0136\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:counter, code:rotation, object:grid_edge, object:sprite, operation:count, operation:rotate, operation:shape_match, operation:translate, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/62593bfd.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/62593bfd.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSort objects to top or bottom edge by whether their shape (up to rotation/flip) is shared.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Several multicolor connected components (8-connected) scattered across the grid.\n\nRule:\n- Compute each object's canonical shape (binary mask, invariant to rotation and flip).\n- Objects whose shape appears in two or more components → translate to TOP edge (row 0).\n- Objects whose shape is unique → translate to BOTTOM edge (row H−h).\n- Horizontal position (left column) is preserved; only vertical translation changes.\n\nKey insight: The sorting criterion is shape frequency (rotation-invariant), not area — duplicated shapes go up, unique shapes go down.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_in_order\",\n  \"src\": \"all connected components (objects) on the background\",\n  \"dst\": \"translate each object d vertically to an edge (x preserved)\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"group objects by their pixel-count (area). If an area value occurs >=2 times, those objects go to the TOP edge; if the area is unique, that object goes to the BOTTOM edge\",\n  \"transform\": \"duplicated-size -> top; singleton-size -> bottom\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"df9fd884\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3309\nmechanism=0.4320\nlexical=0.0140\ncode_feature=0.2857\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:sprite, operation:count, operation:translate, output:same_size, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/df9fd884.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/df9fd884.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nMove the colored object from the lower bracket lane to the upper bracket lane and drop it to the bottom edge.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- One frame color forms exactly two 4-connected bracket objects: a top-edge bracket open downward and a bottom-edge bracket open upward.\n- One other 4-connected foreground object sits in the lower bracket's interior column span.\n\nRule\n- Remove the movable object from its original cells.\n- Keep its shape and color unchanged.\n- Paste it with its bbox columns aligned to the top bracket's interior columns and with its bbox bottom aligned to the grid bottom.\n\nKey insight\n- The lower bracket identifies the object's source lane; the upper bracket provides the target lane, and the final vertical placement is bottom-aligned.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
